PART 4 — Three-Minute Test Notification

Implement a dedicated test notification workflow.

Required behavior

1. When the app is opened, define one app-launch event and schedule a test notification for exactly 3 minutes after that event.
2. Schedule it once per intended test session, not once per screen render.
3. Keep test scheduling separate from production adaptive scheduling.
4. If the app remains open, show an in-app banner and attempt a matching Android system notification.
5. If the app enters the background, let the native scheduler deliver the Android notification when permitted.
6. Persist the unique event ID and delivery state.
7. Prevent duplicate scheduling or display when the user navigates between tabs.
8. On app restart, inspect the persisted event and handle pending or expired events safely.
9. Add a development-only control to send a test notification immediately.
10. Make the delay configurable for development, defaulting to 3 minutes.

For automated testing, use a controllable clock or injectable scheduler so the three-minute behavior can be tested without slowing down the test suite.

Do not accidentally repeat the test notification every three minutes.

If the app is reopened, follow an explicit, documented test-session policy to prevent uncontrolled duplicate test notifications.

