PART 6 — Adaptive Scheduling and Anti-Spam

Use configurable defaults:

- Maximum 3 proactive notifications per day.
- Minimum cooldown between ordinary notifications.
- Quiet hours configurable by the user.
- No routine notification during an active focus session.
- No immediate burst of missed notifications after returning to the app.
- No repeated message until a reasonable portion of the eligible library has been used.
- No repeated reminders for a completed task.
- Deadline messages only when the underlying dates are verified and relevant.
- Reduce low-priority nudges after repeated dismissals or lack of engagement.
- Reset or adapt cooldowns carefully without creating notification storms.

Keep important, time-sensitive reminders distinct from generic motivational nudges.

Randomize within eligible windows, not outside user preferences. Respect local time and quiet hours.

