PART 9 — Testing and Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is complete only when the following have been checked:

1. The library contains at least 120 distinct predefined messages.
2. Every message has a unique ID and valid category.
3. The three-minute test event is scheduled from the defined app-launch event.
4. Navigation does not cause repeated test scheduling.
5. Foreground banner rendering works.
6. Android notification permission handling works.
7. Background local notification delivery is tested on an appropriate device or emulator.
8. Force-stop and battery-restriction limitations are documented.
9. Profile-based message selection works with complete and incomplete profile data.
10. Quiet hours, daily caps, cooldowns, and active-focus suppression work.
11. Recent-message repetition is prevented as expected.
12. Deadline messages never invent dates or countdowns.
13. Notification actions open the correct existing screens.
14. Notification history and settings persist.
15. App restart does not cause notification storms.
16. Build and relevant tests pass.

